WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:04.130
Students meet depth as more is smarter.

2
00:00:04.930 --> 00:00:06.970
Give them a ring a line misses,

3
00:00:07.430 --> 00:00:09.150
and ask which part bent it.

4
00:00:10.330 --> 00:00:13.350
In the seminar: what one neuron can cut,

5
00:00:13.650 --> 00:00:16.250
and why the activation, not the extra

6
00:00:16.250 --> 00:00:18.110
layer alone, does the bending.

7
00:00:19.410 --> 00:00:21.930
A neuron is a weighted sum, a

8
00:00:21.930 --> 00:00:23.510
bias, and an activation.

9
00:00:24.400 --> 00:00:26.580
The weights say how much each

10
00:00:26.580 --> 00:00:29.300
input counts, and the bias shifts

11
00:00:29.300 --> 00:00:31.100
the sum before the bend.

12
00:00:32.280 --> 00:00:35.180
One neuron draws one straight cut.

13
00:00:35.830 --> 00:00:39.310
Stack linear layers with no activation and

14
00:00:39.310 --> 00:00:42.090
they collapse into that same single cut.

15
00:00:43.300 --> 00:00:45.160
The activation is the bend.

16
00:00:45.870 --> 00:00:47.950
It lets the next layer turn the

17
00:00:47.950 --> 00:00:49.690
previous cut into a curve.

18
00:00:50.920 --> 00:00:52.300
Here is a ring.

19
00:00:53.000 --> 00:00:55.280
A line misses it, and a small

20
00:00:55.280 --> 00:00:56.880
network with a hidden layer

21
00:00:56.880 --> 00:00:59.080
learns a boundary around it.

22
00:01:00.230 --> 00:01:00.710
Quick check!

23
00:01:01.350 --> 00:01:04.110
A single neuron draws which boundary?

24
00:01:05.450 --> 00:01:06.930
One straight cut.

25
00:01:07.610 --> 00:01:09.990
A closed curve needs the bend,

26
00:01:10.450 --> 00:01:11.990
and more than one layer.

27
00:01:13.290 --> 00:01:15.830
Have pairs name a shape a line misses

28
00:01:15.830 --> 00:01:17.850
before anyone opens the playground.

29
00:01:18.610 --> 00:01:20.350
Then they run it and say what

30
00:01:20.350 --> 00:01:21.590
the hidden layer added.

31
00:01:22.840 --> 00:01:23.600
Your turn.

32
00:01:24.220 --> 00:01:26.460
Without an activation, what does

33
00:01:26.460 --> 00:01:27.840
a stack of layers become?

34
00:01:29.100 --> 00:01:29.920
Remember this.

35
00:01:30.540 --> 00:01:34.180
One neuron makes one cut, and depth

36
00:01:34.180 --> 00:01:36.300
bends the boundary only when an

37
00:01:36.300 --> 00:01:38.540
activation sits between the layers.

38
00:01:39.840 --> 00:01:41.160
Try it in your next lecture.

39
00:01:41.840 --> 00:01:44.460
One phone between two, and the sentence

40
00:01:44.460 --> 00:01:47.220
you will mark is what the activation does.
